Project Plan: Poverty and Educational Attainment in Montgomery County, Maryland

Data:

The primary data for this project will come from three datasets I picked out, most of 
which are focused on educational outcomes and other socioeconomic indicators. The information 
in these datasets is drawn from Maryland communities, either from Montgomery County 
exclusively, or county-wide across the state. 

Dataset 1:

The first dataset comes from the Maryland Open Data portal. This dataset contains many 
important socioeconomic factors, all of which will be helpful for identifying poverty across 
Maryland. This dataset also contains information based on multiple counties across Maryland, 
rather than being limited to just Montgomery County. Some of the key variables include, poverty 
rate, median income, unemployment rate, and several different variables that contain informaiton 
regarding educational attainment. The primary use of this dataset will be to run a comparative
analysis across Maryland counties, likely to study wealthy areas next to poverty stricken areas, 
along with different demographics. 

The dataset can be accessed here: https://opendata.maryland.gov/Demographic/Maryland-
Counties-Socioeconomic-Characteristics-AC/is7h-kp6x/about_data

Despite how rich this dataset is with information, there are still some limits. One issue would be 
that there is no specification for schools across each district, which would be extremely helpful. 
On top of that, there will also need to be filtering done to make sure there is consistency in the 
data over the years. Even with these limitations though, the dataset is generally still a strong one.

Dataset 2:

The second dataset I was able to access comes from Datacensus.gov. Most of its data is 
sourced from the U.S census American Community Survey. Essentially, this dataset takes a look 
at the poverty rates, income levels, and general demographic characteristics for Montgomery 
County. This dataset will be used to provide most of the poverty and income indicators in the 
project. The key variables used would be poverty rates, child poverty rate, median household 
income, and adults without high school diplomas. 

The dataset can be accessed at: 
https://data.census.gov/table/ACSST5Y2022.S1701?q=Montgomery+County+Maryland+povert
y



Although this dataset provides valuable insight for Montgomery County specifically, 
there are a couple of issues that come with it as well. Similar to the previous dataset, the data is 
not linked to specific schools, which would be helpful to know when coming up with solutions. 
Though I do have access to a dataset with school-wide information, using both of these datasets 
will require some alignment. However, even with these issues, the dataset is still very helpful. 

Dataset 3:

The third dataset took a little bit of digging to find, but does have valuable information. I 
was able to find it directly on the Montgomery County Public Schools website. It contains many 
details about high schools in Montgomery County. Some of the key variables are graduation 
rates, dropout rates, attendance rates, and FARM (Free and Reduced Meals) participation. This 
dataset will be a primary source of information for the project, given its data on educational 
outcomes like graduation rates. 

The dataset can be downloaded here: https://www.montgomeryschoolsmd.org/school-profiles

This is a relatively small dataset, so it does come with a few issues. For one, the time-
span is very limited, which could narrow down the project. There is also a lack of detail when it 
comes to demographics. However, with the help of the other two datasets, it is possible to work 
around these issues to answer the project questions. 

Research Goals and Questions:

The primary goal of this project is to analyze how poverty and economic disadvantages 
impact high school graduation rates in Montgomery County, and to compare these relationships 
to other areas across Maryland. 

Questions, and (potentially) how to go about answering them: 

1. How strongly are poverty indicators associated with high school graduation rates in 
Montgomery County?
a. I will answer this question by doing a correlation analysis and linear regression 
between the variables of poverty rate (from the second dataset) and graduation 
rates (the MCPS dataset)
2. How does this relationship compare across different counties in Maryland?
a. I will do a cross-county regression for dataset 3, and to visualize the answer I will 
make scatterplots.
3. How does this relationship change when accounting for factors like race/ethnicity and 
demographics?
a. Multiple regression including demographic control variables. 
4. Are there specific geographic areas where poverty is linked to lower graduation rates?
a. Using dataset 2, I will create heatmaps to visualize this relationship.
5. Can income indicators predict graduation outcomes?
a. A regression model 
a. Correlation and simple linear regression using dataset 3.
a. Correlation and regression between dropout rates and poverty indicators, possibly 
a graph as well.
a. Multivariate regression, while having attendance as an intermediate variable.
a. Compare means and make visualization of differences with bar graphs. 
6. What is the relationship between FARM participation and graduation rates?
7. Do schools with a higher dropout rate also show stronger links to poverty?
8. How does attendance rate relate to both poverty, and graduation rates?
9. How does Montgomery County compare to state averages in educational equity?
